msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:61 977c299780024d71825f6a63727a2f24
msgid ""
"Get detailed information about a specific concept from a BioPortal "
"ontology, including full defin..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst 499de562aad645818afbdb39c2a1bb80
msgid "BioPortal_get_concept tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:67 440688995ba74b27a47b4548860611a6
msgid "**Name**: ``BioPortal_get_concept``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:69 6ae6b47d74334c84b4412741399b0c0a
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get detailed information about a specific concept from a"
" BioPortal ontology, including full definition, synonyms, CUI codes, and "
"semantic types. Requires knowing the ontology acronym and concept IRI. "
"Use BioPortal\\_search\\_ontology\\_terms first to find concept IDs, then"
" use this tool for complete details. Example: get details for DOID:1909 "
"(melanoma) from the DOID ontology, or GO:0006915 (apoptotic process) from"
" the GO ontology."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:73 59b41de2c4f042029f9ff4c1a9bd075a
msgid ""
"``ontology`` (string) (required) Ontology acronym in BioPortal. Examples:"
" 'GO', 'HP', 'DOID', 'CHEBI', 'UBERON', 'NCIT', 'MESH', 'SNOMEDCT', "
"'RXNORM'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:76 76b952c4613249cf8104126d360eb47d
msgid ""
"``concept_id`` (string) (required) Full IRI of the concept. Examples: "
"'http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID\\_1909', "
"'http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO\\_0006915', "
"'http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP\\_0001250'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:94 845145a65450408ea10588e574c39a5b
msgid "**BioPortal_get_hierarchy** (Type: BioPortalTool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:96 37a1e8e2242f4a0f991f5ed19ea8f3f7
msgid ""
"Get children, parents, or ancestors of a specific concept in a BioPortal "
"ontology. Enables hierar..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst 96cff377a6ce4c6787277cf71c5a25dd
msgid "BioPortal_get_hierarchy tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:102 e8db61ecb5a949acbd2278d87a01dc46
msgid "**Name**: ``BioPortal_get_hierarchy``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:104 2d1ef1a936d5453d97216183efa59cd4
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get children, parents, or ancestors of a specific "
"concept in a BioPortal ontology. Enables hierarchical browsing of "
"ontology term relationships (is-a hierarchy). Use to explore narrower "
"terms (children), broader terms (parents), or full ancestry path "
"(ancestors). Example: get children of DOID:9351 (diabetes mellitus) to "
"find type 1, type 2, gestational diabetes; get ancestors of HP:0001250 "
"(Seizure) to see the full path to root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:108 4d689568c9e541a9815b17f5a232133c
msgid ""
"``ontology`` (string) (required) Ontology acronym in BioPortal. Examples:"
" 'GO', 'HP', 'DOID', 'CHEBI', 'UBERON', 'NCIT'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:111 dee6ecb6acba46ad88d63121e774adf4
msgid ""
"``concept_id`` (string) (required) Full IRI of the concept. Example: "
"'http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID\\_9351' for diabetes mellitus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:114 020b977c32314ec38190354585dcd7d2
msgid ""
"``direction`` (string, null) (optional) Direction of hierarchy traversal:"
" 'children' (narrower terms, default), 'parents' (direct broader terms), "
"or 'ancestors' (all broader terms to root)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:117 70a7e303b28342daba079f4c53e3fb07
msgid ""
"``page_size`` (integer, null) (optional) Number of results to return "
"(default: 25, max: 100)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:135 3c670872516e41e381453968c352d5d0
msgid "**BioPortal_search_ontology_terms** (Type: BioPortalTool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:137 f72b5b96951445b1832bafc5197fbf69
msgid ""
"Search across 900+ biomedical ontologies in BioPortal (NCBO) for concepts"
" matching a query. BioPo..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst ea67b953d62e4cd98bfdfee3bdc69ac8
msgid "BioPortal_search_ontology_terms tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:143 1ccad953e01040dfaf20757f9306abf5
msgid "**Name**: ``BioPortal_search_ontology_terms``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:145 ee969c1f7ca441b18f8393ac2898e09e
msgid ""
"**Description**: Search across 900+ biomedical ontologies in BioPortal "
"(NCBO) for concepts matching a query. BioPortal is the world's largest "
"repository of biomedical ontologies including GO (gene function), HPO "
"(phenotypes), DOID (diseases), CHEBI (chemicals), UBERON (anatomy), "
"SNOMED, MeSH, and 900+ more. Returns matching concepts with labels, IDs, "
"definitions, and synonyms. Optionally filter by specific ontologies. "
"Example: search 'melanoma' to find disease terms across DOID, NCIT, MESH,"
" SNOMED; search 'apoptosis' in GO ontology for programmed cell death "
"terms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:149 ee9d485331d646059ba47aecb0f63470
msgid ""
"``query`` (string) (required) Search query for finding ontology terms. "
"Can be disease names, gene functions, phenotypes, chemical names, "
"anatomical terms, etc. Examples: 'melanoma', 'apoptosis', 'seizure', "
"'aspirin', 'hippocampus'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:152 31ef47bc80ce40b6bd5d91db3ea9198e
msgid ""
"``ontologies`` (string, null) (optional) Comma-separated list of ontology"
" acronyms to search within. If null, searches all ontologies. Common "
"ontologies: GO (Gene Ontology), HP (Human Phenotype), DOID (Disease "
"Ontology), CHEBI (Chemical Entities), UBERON (Anatomy), NCIT (NCI "
"Thesaurus), MESH (Medical Subject Headings), SNOMEDCT (SNOMED CT), RXNORM"
" (Drug Names)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:155 d16344811326461cbc412693f2b7e832
msgid ""
"``page_size`` (integer, null) (optional) Number of results to return "
"(default: 10, max: 50)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/bioportal_tools.rst:158 7c3d6188e18a49fbb66b0e0236e166e3
msgid ""
"``exact_match`` (boolean, null) (optional) If true, only return exact "
"matches (default: false)."
msgstr ""

